This MC simulation for dodecane uses the flip protocol for all
CCCC dihedral angles - see the gaszmat file.
A standard MC simulation is run otherwise with 2M configurations
of averaging after 1M for equilibration.
Execution time: ca. 15 min on a 2.4 GHz Pentium IV.

Note the symmetry of the resultant dihedral angle distributions
for the flipped dihedrals in comparison to those from the
the 5X longer run in the dodeca10M directory.
